// ADR-009 C3 #14 slice 2 (S2d) — the API-INSTALLED weave RUNTIME SMOKE,
// AGGREGATE-carrier shape: the COMPILER-GENERATED specialization path (not
// the S1a hand-written proxy). A real annotation handler installs a
// polymorphic BEFORE template (with a scalar capture) and a concrete AFTER
// template through the PUBLIC comptime API (before_hook / after_hook /
// capture / install); the S2c weave generates the wrapper + hygienic impl
// shadow.
//
// MEASURED STATUS (S2d, RE-MEASURED S7) — NAMED-EXPECTED-FALLBACK (the
// C3-G6 Deep-contingency pin shape, loud-flip semantics; see the CLI cell):
// the heterogeneous 2-ary target forces the G9 compiler-internal MUTATION
// AGGREGATE. Of the two S2d-measured gaps in its inline-Object annotation
// chain, S7 CLOSED gap (a) — `classify_type_annotation_metadata` gained
// its `TypeAnnotation::Object` return-kind arm, so the specialized handler
// now carries a proven FrameDescriptor.return_kind and the original W36
// stop no longer fires (the cell's loud-flip caught the identity change).
// Gap (b) remains OPEN and is the re-pinned identity — MirToIR has no
// statically proven field layout for `Place::Field` reads off an
// inline-Object-annotated local (`unresolved direct field read .a0`);
// issue #70 carries both measurements verbatim + the close condition.
// VM and JIT agree on stdout (whole-program interpreter fallback, LOUD,
// never silent); the SINGLE-carrier sibling
// (`c3-api-installed-hooks-single.shape`) is zero-fallback native, and the
// USER-DECLARED `type` spelling of the same aggregate is zero-fallback
// native (the S1a cells), attributing the residual gap to the
// inline-schema spelling exactly. The CLI cell fails loudly the moment
// the fallback disappears, forcing the flip to the zero-fallback form.
//
// Heterogeneous 2-ary (int, number) target; hot loop of 200 calls crosses
// T1@100 (crates/shape-vm/src/tier.rs). The annotation `comptime post`
// handler is NOT a top-level comptime block (the parse-based vacuity guard
// distinguishes exactly this).
//
// Value-distinguishing arithmetic (the S1a 40x00-style convention), per call
// i in 0..200 with b = 2.5:
//   before: a0 = 2i + 1 (x2 + capture bump 1), a1 = 2.5 typed-preserved
//   impl:   b > 2.0 holds → a0 * 10 = 20i + 10
//   after:  + 3 → 20i + 13;  sum = 20*19900 + 13*200 = 400600
// Expected stdout: 400600
//   skipped before          → sum 10i+3   = 199600
//   skipped after           → sum 20i+10  = 400000
//   number slot kind-corrupt (b fails > 2.0) → sum 2i+4 = 40600
fn boost<Args>(args: Args, bump: int) -> Args {
  args[0] = args[0] * 2 + bump
  return args
}
fn settle(r: int) -> int { return r + 3 }

annotation hooked() on function {
  comptime post(target, ctx) {
    install(before_hook(boost, [capture("bump", 1)]))
    install(after_hook(settle, []))
  }
}

@hooked()
fn calc(a: int, b: number) -> int {
  if b > 2.0 { a * 10 } else { a }
}

fn run() -> int {
  let mut total = 0
  for i in 0..200 { total = total + calc(i, 2.5) }
  total
}
print(run())
